<p>I don't wanna clog up the thread much, because this is more difference of opinions, but for me, the crux of this is this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Transcendent identity disorder:</span> This mental disorder was discovered by Foundation researchers in the early 1960s. Indistinguishable from scientifically-understood dissociative identity disorder for medical professionals outside of the Foundation,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In-universe, it's a mental disorder, and cannot be distinguished from DID by professionals who don't work in the Foundation. I interpret this to be trying to play a (fictional, and also analogous to real-world) mental disorder for horror. I am not a fan of that, and even taken solely in the context of this article and the Foundationverse alone, it's underwhelming to what the article builds up to prior to this bit, and seems to set up only for (admittedly creepy) notes in the addendum after. This is one thing I am not a fan of.</p>

