<p>I think it's because the examples provided as big flashing signs of these effects are so super small-scale. A no-confidence vote and a two-seat change in an election (from two different countries, 33 years apart) are fairly minuscule effects (assuming those actions are in fact due to the effects of 2798). Minor political shakeups happen all the time, everywhere, and I didn't see anything that made me go &quot;Uh oh!&quot;.</p>
