			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2447405">
									

<blockquote>
<p>We honestly don't know and so anyone with an opinion one way or another is suspect, to me, without lots of evidence to back the argument up.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The resulting paradox seems self-evident to me. If everyone has someone else's perceptions, then cooperation (ultimately as a hive mind) is required for survival, but if people are also incapable of believing that cooperation is possible then the result would seem to be extinction.</p>

